# Coding Guidelines

## Avoid Hasty Abstractions

We want abstraction especially for reusable systems to avoid duplicate code.
However, do not make early or pre-mature assumptions. For example, only add function parameters that are actually used by its callers. When the time comes that we need more params, only then should we add them.

## Performance

We want to prioritize performance over realistic physics and accuracy. Remember that this is a 2D pixel-art game so as long as it feels good, we don't need to make the graphics/maths/collissions extremely accurate and precise.

## Code Architecture

This project uses an ECS or entity-component-system architecture.
Always use existing entities/components/systems and extend them or create new ones when possible.
The knife library handles the ECS system of this game.

## Tweening & Easing

Always use the **flux** library for tweening and easing functions.
Use xxxFlux to store the flux instance if needed.
Example:
```lua
targetFlux = flux.to(self, duration, { x = targetX }):ease("quadout")
```
